    "annotations": [
      {
        "id": "a1",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Propulsion (bond graph, one chain per rotor).** Electrical 1-junction: the winding voltage (MSe, set by the rotor-speed governor), the winding and drive losses (R), a current detector (Df) and the motor gyrator (GY, k_t). Shaft 1-junction at the rotor speed relative to the airframe: the motor, the rotor's axial momentum (Rotor3D, bonded to the airframe body: its torque reaction and gyroscopic moment act on the airframe) and the blade-element/momentum aerodynamics (RotorBEMT, a nonlinear R). The thrust, H-force and hub moments act on the airframe at the hub (Hub mount + HubWrench). The lower rotor sees the upper rotor's uniform inflow (AeroU.v0 -> AeroL.vext).",
        "x": 200,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 1100,
        "h": 90,
        "color": "blue"
      },
      {
        "id": "a2",
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "**Rotor stand (JPL 25-ft Space Simulator).** The coaxial rotor on a fixed stand in CO2 at 0.0175 kg/m^3 and 2600 rpm (Koning et al. 2019). StandControl steps the thrust coefficient through the measured range (a PI on the symmetric collective), trims the pair torque-free (differential collective), then applies 5 deg cyclic steps on the lower rotor, the system-identification sequence of Grip et al. (2017) Fig. 15.",
        "x": 20,
        "y": -120,
        "w": 900,
        "h": 70,
        "color": "blue"
      }
    ]
  },
